[5.715157, "o", "\u001b[32m  ↳ completed\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[33m⚙ tool_call\u001b[0m Read /tmp/calc-98plp0ac/test_calc.py \u001b[2m[read, pending]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.71567, "o", "\u001b[32m  ↳ completed\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.425501, "o", "`average()` in `calc.py` adds a stray `+ 1` to the mean, so `average([2, 4, 6])` returns `5.0` when it should return `4`. `test_calc.py` asserts that the result equals `4`, so that off-by-one fails the test. (I didn't run it; this is from reading the code.)"]
[10.238121, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m[end_turn]\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36myou ›\u001b[0m Fix the bug in calc.py, then run python3 -m unittest -q in my workspace to confirm.\r\n\u001b[1mviktor ›\u001b[0m "]
